{"parentUuid":"9533fa69-bc19-45b7-8937-a6b9210d433a","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/forni/Development/handld-quote-viewer","sessionId":"6995d898-23e9-42e6-9a84-971bd10a25cd","version":"1.0.102","gitBranch":"rebuild","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CfZYja8mCeL5s7fvJxZoCR","type":"tool_result","content":"Based on the provided documentation, there is no explicit mechanism for command inheritance or referencing global commands from local command files. The documentation describes two types of commands:\n\n1. Project commands (stored in `.claude/commands/`)\n2. Personal commands (stored in `~/.claude/commands/`)\n\nThe text notes that \"Conflicts between user and project level commands are not supported\" and multiple commands with the same base filename cannot coexist. \n\nThe closest feature to inheritance is namespacing, where commands can be \"Organize[d] in subdirectories\" with the subdirectory name appearing in the command description. However, this does not provide true command inheritance or global reference capabilities.\n\nTo avoid duplication, users would need to manually manage their command files across project and personal directories."}]},"uuid":"1bddef41-c7f7-4521-b72b-e0e0da2d8393","timestamp":"2025-09-03T16:12:02.296Z","toolUseResult":{"bytes":2247600,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"Based on the provided documentation, there is no explicit mechanism for command inheritance or referencing global commands from local command files. The documentation describes two types of commands:\n\n1. Project commands (stored in `.claude/commands/`)\n2. Personal commands (stored in `~/.claude/commands/`)\n\nThe text notes that \"Conflicts between user and project level commands are not supported\" and multiple commands with the same base filename cannot coexist. \n\nThe closest feature to inheritance is namespacing, where commands can be \"Organize[d] in subdirectories\" with the subdirectory name appearing in the command description. However, this does not provide true command inheritance or global reference capabilities.\n\nTo avoid duplication, users would need to manually manage their command files across project and personal directories.","durationMs":8782,"url":"https://docs.anthropic.com/en/docs/claude-code/slash-commands"}}
